      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A mild and efficient method for the synthesis of unsymmetrical diaryl- and triarylmethanes through a B(C6F5)3 catalyzed reduction of para-quinone methides and fuchsones respectively, using the Hantzsch ester as a reducing source has been developed. Detailed mechanistic investigations revealed that the reaction actually proceeds through a Lewis acid-base pair complex derived from B(C6F5)3 and the Hantzsch ester."},
